 "provenance": {
  "source_type": "literature",
  "citation": "Ruan et al. Potentiators empower synthetic microbiomes as silent guardians against co-contamination. Nature Communications (2025). DOI: 10.1038/s41467-025-67953-5. [PMC12858907]",
  "doi": "10.1038/s41467-025-67953-5",
  "url": "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC12858907/",
  "notes": "Full recipe recovered from the primary literature: base medium 'Minimal (mineral salts) medium MM' (Supplementary Information / Supplementary Methods of the source paper itself: 'Potentiators empower synthetic microbiomes as silent guardians against co-contamination', Nature Communications (2025), DOI 10.1038/s41467-025-67953-5; PMC12858907. The MM recipe is defined verbatim in the Supplementary Methods (Media section).). Extracted from the primary paper (snippet: mixed carbon sources (25 mmol/g",
  "verification": "paper-verified (complete recipe; cited + supplementary sources chased)",
  "verification_evidence": "MM with 25 mmol/gDW each of glucose, citrate, acetate, and fumarate (quadruple carbon sources, C = 4).",
  "verification_confidence": "high",
  "recipe_evidence": "MM base (verbatim, Supplementary Methods): 'The minimal medium medium (MM) consisted of 1 g/L NaCl, 1 g/L NH4Cl, 1.5 g/L K2HPO4, 0.5 g/L KH2PO4, and 0.2 g/L MgSO4·7H2O.' Carbon-source configuration (verbatim): 'C = 4 condition: Four carbon sources were included, each at 25 mmol to ensure balanced representation: 25 mmol glucose ... 25 mmol citrate ... 25 mmol acetate ... and 25 mmol fumarate ...' Simulation flux settings (verbatim): 'While NH4+ still had an LB of 100 mmol/gDW, all other organic substances had an LB of 0 mmol/gDW, and all other inorganic substances without C/N had an LB of 1000",
  "recipe_confidence": "high",
  "base_medium": "Minimal (mineral salts) medium MM: 1 g/L NaCl, 1 g/L NH4Cl, 1.5 g/L K2HPO4, 0.5 g/L KH2PO4, 0.2 g/L MgSO4·7H2O (Supplementary Method 1). In-silico for the SuperCC/GSMM C=4 condition, supplemented with 25 mmol/gDW each of glucose, citrate, acetate, and fumarate.",
  "base_medium_reference": "Supplementary Information / Supplementary Methods of the source paper itself: 'Potentiators empower synthetic microbiomes as silent guardians against co-contamination', Nature Communications (2025), DOI 10.1038/s41467-025-67953-5; PMC12858907. The MM recipe is defined verbatim in the Supplementary Methods (Media section).",
  "recuration": {
   "date": "2026-07-16",
   "round": "complete-recipe (cited+supplementary chased)",
   "status": "corrected",
   "confidence": "high",
   "sources_chased": [
    {
     "what": "Base physical MM recipe (referenced as Supplementary Methods / Media section)",
     "obtained": true,
     "how": "Downloaded EuropePMC supplementaryFiles zip -> 41467_2025_67953_MOESM1_ESM.pdf (Supplementary Information), extracted 'Supplementary Method 1. Media'",
     "added": [
      "NaCl 1 g/L",
      "NH4Cl 1 g/L",
      "K2HPO4 1.5 g/L",
      "KH2PO4 0.5 g/L (monopotassium phosphate, previously folded into dipotassium phosphate)",
      "MgSO4·7H2O 0.2 g/L",
      "confirmed MM contains NO trace-elements solution and NO vitamins"
