    }
   ],
   "missing_before": [
    "monopotassium phosphate (KH2PO4, the second/acidic phosphate buffer salt — only dipotassium phosphate was represented before)"
   ],
   "corrections": [],
   "notes": "Complete recipe recovered from the paper's own Supplementary Method 1 (Media). The physical MM is a bare mineral-salts medium (NaCl, NH4Cl, K2HPO4, KH2PO4, MgSO4·7H2O) with NO trace-element mix, NO vitamins, NO added carbon in the base — distinct from the EM/DM media in the same paper, which DO carry a 1 mL/L trace-elements solution (FeSO4, MgSO4, CoCl2, ZnSO4, MnCl2, CuSO4, EDTA). The current exchange set was already chemically complete at the ion level (Na, Cl, K, pi, Mg, SO4, NH4, O2 + 4 carbons); this curation adds the actual salt identities/concentrations, splits phosphate into K2HPO4+KH2"
  },
